 "preferred_name": "Applied element method",
 "kind": "method",
 "definition": "A numerical method in structural engineering that models a structure as small rigid elements joined by springs, so that its behaviour can be simulated up to collapse.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A numerical analysis method for predicting the continuum and discrete behavior of structures. It uses discrete cracking to automatically track structural collapse through stages from elastic behavior to element separation and collision.",
